### execute-task

Read the `{{ $baseDir }}/{{ $taskFileName }}` file and identify every uncompleted task (lines starting with `- [ ]`). You MUST process each uncompleted task one at a time, completing all of the steps below for one task before moving on to the next. Do NOT skip any tasks.

For each uncompleted task, perform the following steps in order:

1. **State the task** — Print which task you are currently working on (e.g. "Task 2: <task description>") so the developer can track progress.
2. **Do the work** — Implement the changes described by the task. Follow existing code conventions and patterns.
3. **Run existing tests** — Run the project's test suite after every change to verify no regressions were introduced. If any test fails, fix the issue before proceeding.
4. **Mark the task complete** — After the work is done and tests pass, tick the task checkbox as completed in `{{ $baseDir }}/{{ $taskFileName }}`.

Move on to the next uncompleted task and repeat steps 1–4. Continue until every uncompleted task has been processed.

After all tasks have been processed, run the full test suite. Print a final summary listing each task and its status. If any tests fail, suggest a rollback to the task-plan phase.

#### Criteria

For EACH uncompleted task:
- [ ] Work completed as described
- [ ] Existing tests pass (no regressions)
- [ ] Task checkbox marked complete

All uncompleted tasks processed:
- [ ] Every uncompleted task in `{{ $taskFileName }}` has been completed
- [ ] Full test suite passes
